1
00:03:34,400 --> 00:03:37,540
Hello, Michigan.

2
00:03:37,540 --> 00:03:39,110
Wow.

3
00:03:39,120 --> 00:03:42,037
Well, my friends, it's been quite a night.

4
00:03:42,047 --> 00:03:51,391
I think it's been a really great night for Democrats all across the country and right here in Michigan.

5
00:03:51,880 --> 00:03:58,370
The voters of Michigan have spoken in recordbreaking turnout.

6
00:03:58,370 --> 00:04:04,040
And I am honored to stand before you as the next governor of Michigan.

7
00:04:11,240 --> 00:04:18,452
And I am equally thrilled that I will be heading to Lancing with a Democratic trifecta.

8
00:04:21,895 --> 00:04:30,410
Listen, for 22 months, I have been asking you one question.

9
00:04:31,030 --> 00:04:33,250
Who do you want your leaders to work for?

10
00:04:33,970 --> 00:04:38,590
And my friends, the voters of Michigan have answered loud and clear.

11
00:04:39,330 --> 00:04:44,070
They want leaders who will work for you and every person in the state of Michigan.

12
00:04:48,050 --> 00:04:53,070
In this election, from the western reaches of the upper peninsula to downtown Detroit,

13
00:04:53,290 --> 00:04:54,670
Voters sent a clear message.

14
00:04:55,130 --> 00:04:59,910
They want leaders who will fight for them, fight to lower costs, fight to grow our economy,

15
00:05:00,370 --> 00:05:04,510
Fight the corruption that too often protects the pe powerful and hurts the people.

16
00:05:04,730 --> 00:05:13,010
And in this election, we showed the nation that in our democracy, the power of the people will always rule the day.

17
00:05:21,130 --> 00:05:26,030
My friend, this is this win is a victory for every one of us.

18
00:05:26,190 --> 00:05:30,870
Every Michigander like my friend Gwen and so many others.

19
00:05:32,000 --> 00:05:35,270
It's so beautiful to see you tonight.

20
00:05:35,280 --> 00:05:38,710
My friend Gwen has to look at her bills every night and wonder how to make ends meet.

21
00:05:38,710 --> 00:05:41,230
And I know so many Michiganers feel that same way.

22
00:05:41,490 --> 00:05:45,210
But Gwen, tonight this is a victory for you and all of us.

23
00:05:45,440 --> 00:05:47,143
Thank you.

24
00:05:47,143 --> 00:05:51,180
It is a win for our kids.

25
00:05:51,180 --> 00:06:02,440
Our kids who deserve to grow up in a state that is the best place in the nation to call home.

26
00:06:03,100 --> 00:06:10,680
And it is a win for our young girls who tonight can look up and for the first time in our state's history,

27
00:06:10,949 --> 00:06:16,720
For the first time in our state's history, see two women leading this state.

28
00:06:19,207 --> 00:06:29,520
As governor and lieutenant governor, who will work together every day to ensure that young girls and women always have access to the health

29
00:06:29,520 --> 00:06:34,304
Care they need and the rights and freedoms they deserve.

30
00:06:34,304 --> 00:06:41,830
And my friends, it's also a win for democracy because our Democratic trifecta.

31
00:06:43,360 --> 00:06:44,850
Feels good to say that, doesn't it?

32
00:06:45,170 --> 00:06:55,690
Our Democratic trifecta is going to go to Lancing and pass a voting rights act for the state of Michigan to ensure that every

33
00:06:55,690 --> 00:07:00,090
Citizen in this state is protected at the ballot box in every election.

34
00:07:04,040 --> 00:07:06,380
Tonight, I just want to say thank you.

35
00:07:06,780 --> 00:07:12,457
Thank you to those of you who stayed here much longer and many longer hours than you might have thought,

36
00:07:12,740 --> 00:07:18,420
But who worked also for days and months in the better part of two years to knock doors,

37
00:07:18,640 --> 00:07:23,580
Make phone calls, have thousands of conversations with voters in all 83 counties.

38
00:07:24,260 --> 00:07:25,860
This win is for you.

39
00:07:26,240 --> 00:07:35,620
And I want to a special note to the hardest working campaign staff in the business.

40
00:07:36,000 --> 00:07:45,720
An incredible group of people led by women, including my day one campaign manager,

41
00:07:46,439 --> 00:07:56,760
Nikki Goldshine, and the best communications policy deputy campaign manager in the nation, Alyssa Bradley.

42
00:08:00,030 --> 00:08:05,470
They along with so many of our teams from Jesse to Ashley to Wes to Alec to Mary.

43
00:08:05,710 --> 00:08:06,530
I love all of you.

44
00:08:06,990 --> 00:08:08,130
You worked the long nights.

45
00:08:08,250 --> 00:08:12,090
You took on the tough challenges and you never stopped believing in our mission.

46
00:08:12,350 --> 00:08:16,810
Your work, your dedication, your commitment, made this victory possible.

47
00:08:16,810 --> 00:08:23,661
And I hope everyone takes a moment tonight to be proud of what we've all accomplished together.

48
00:08:25,020 --> 00:08:30,749
To Winnie Brinks, our incredible lieutenant governor elect.

49
00:08:30,749 --> 00:08:37,810
Together, we've made history and with you as my partner, we are going to deliver for the state of Michigan.

50
00:08:38,890 --> 00:08:43,470
And finally, to my family, you know, this campaign was quite a journey.

51
00:08:44,190 --> 00:08:46,930
It wasn't always an easy one, but on the good days and the bad,

52
00:08:47,070 --> 00:08:48,790
You were always there to light the way forward.

53
00:08:49,550 --> 00:08:54,050
In Ryan, you will have the first spouse of a governor in state history who is a combat veteran.

54
00:08:55,796 --> 00:09:02,960
And in Aiden, you will have a first kid who reminds us every day why this fight matters.

55
00:09:14,990 --> 00:09:19,810
Like all of you, we know that every family deserves the chance to keep their loved ones happy,

56
00:09:20,010 --> 00:09:21,350
Healthy, safe, and thriving.

57
00:09:21,810 --> 00:09:24,990
And every child deserves a future that is limitless.

58
00:09:25,328 --> 00:09:28,650
Michigan, we're gonna build that future for all of our kids together.

59
00:09:29,690 --> 00:09:33,350
And now the we are and now the work begins.

60
00:09:33,350 --> 00:09:35,250
The challenges ahead are serious.

61
00:09:35,570 --> 00:09:40,731
There will be disagreements, difficult decisions, and days when the work feels harder than we imagined.

62
00:09:40,850 --> 00:09:46,130
But I know what Michiganers can accomplish when we come together around a common purpose.

63
00:09:46,870 --> 00:09:52,930
Because because here in Michigan, I will because here in Michigan, we lead.

64
00:09:53,150 --> 00:09:54,390
We put the world on wheels.

65
00:09:54,670 --> 00:09:55,690
We built the middle class.

66
00:09:56,130 --> 00:09:57,546
We built the Meno Bridge.

67
00:09:57,690 --> 00:10:03,392
A constant reminder that we can do big transformational things when we work together.

68
00:10:04,630 --> 00:10:10,910
And look, you all know I will proudly work with anyone who is ready to deliver for the people of Michigan.

69
00:10:11,630 --> 00:10:16,230
But make no mistake, I will be unafraid to stand up to any bully,

70
00:10:16,710 --> 00:10:32,030
No matter how powerful, who brings chaos to our communities or tries to put their profits ahead of our people or threatens the rights

71
00:10:32,030 --> 00:10:33,751
Or freedoms of Michiganders.

72
00:10:34,130 --> 00:10:36,190
Because I will always fight for you.

73
00:10:36,710 --> 00:10:41,170
No matter who you are, where you live, how you pray, or how you vote.

74
00:10:47,460 --> 00:10:51,500
So tonight, you've given us the opportunity to build a Michigan that works for everyone.

75
00:10:51,900 --> 00:10:55,540
With communities full of people who are ready to roll up their sleeves and get to work,

76
00:10:55,946 --> 00:10:59,600
Winnie Brinks and I, as the first team of women in history leading the state,

77
00:10:59,600 --> 00:11:01,040
Will carry the work forward.

78
00:11:01,557 --> 00:11:09,360
Will carry the work forward of the women who came before us, including Gretchen Whitmer,

79
00:11:09,360 --> 00:11:16,550
Who I want to say a particular thank you to, for your leadership and love for the state of Michigan,

80
00:11:16,550 --> 00:11:18,070
And for your friendship and support.

81
00:11:19,090 --> 00:11:22,250
And to every Michigander waiting for government to make a difference in your life,

82
00:11:22,250 --> 00:11:23,630
We're ready to get to work for you.

83
00:11:23,770 --> 00:11:24,550
Let's lower costs.

84
00:11:24,790 --> 00:11:25,650
Let's raise our wages.

85
00:11:25,890 --> 00:11:26,590
Let's end corruption.

86
00:11:26,970 --> 00:11:30,750
Let's make Michigan the best place in the nation to call home.

87
00:11:31,499 --> 00:11:32,987
Let's get it done.

88
00:11:32,987 --> 00:11:36,990
Thank you everyone and good night.
